                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17170155" author="moon" created="Mon, 3 Aug 2020 16:21:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;How do you add packages to remote interpreter? Through &quot;spark.jars.packages&quot; spark configuration property or another way?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17170184" author="alexott" created="Mon, 3 Aug 2020 16:47:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve seen some occasions when spark.jars.packages wasn&apos;t enough and was need to add same coordinates into &quot;Dependencies&quot; section...&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17170426" author="reamer" created="Mon, 3 Aug 2020 20:56:14 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I need a more general approach. Also the JDBC interpreter needs some additional jars (e.g. ojdbc)&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17172104" author="zjffdu" created="Thu, 6 Aug 2020 07:59:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=Reamer&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;Reamer&quot;&gt;Reamer&lt;/a&gt;&#160;In yarn mode,&#160; I just need to configure spark interpreter via inline configuration.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13009171/13009171_image-2020-08-06-15-59-27-263.png&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17172507" author="moon" created="Thu, 6 Aug 2020 16:19:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;ah, now I understand the problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;To me, &quot;Zeppelin Sync&quot; sounds better than using &quot;ReadWriteMany Storage&quot;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Configuration point of view, like you summarized &quot;Zeppelin Sync&quot; should work out of the box, but &quot;ReadWriteMany&quot; requires storage configuration, and the storage configuration can be quite a challenge many users. (from the installation of storage to securing NFS/etc).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In performance point of view, if &quot;Zeppeiln Sync&quot; can be implemented in a way that ZeppelinServer download artifacts from a maven repo(which can be slow) and each interpreter Pod sync the artifacts from ZeppelinServer (network between pod will be much faster), then there will be not much performance penalty compare to&#160; &quot;ReadWriteMany Storage&quot; while most ReadWriteMany storage also needs to transfer all artifacts through the network.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Implementation point of view, one way is make two additional http endpoints in ZeppelinServer side, one for a list of files in local-repository, another for transferring a file in a local-repository. So interpreter.sh can copy artifacts through the network before it starts the RemoteInterpreterServer process. Do you have other solutions in mind?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17174396" author="reamer" created="Mon, 10 Aug 2020 15:42:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Hi &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=moon&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;moon&quot;&gt;moon&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
You are right, NFS and other storage solutions are quite a challenge. I had some troubles with the locking mechanic of Maven in conjunction with NFS(&lt;a href=&quot;https://stackoverflow.com/questions/43747117/maven-can-create-folders-and-lock-file-but-hangs-while-downloading&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;maven-can-create-folders-and-lock-file-but-hangs-while-downloading&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At the end of last week I finally found a working solution with NFS. If anyone is interested in the solution, these are my changes to interpreter.spec&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeHeader panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;interpreter.spec&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ spec:
   containers:
   - name: {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.container.name}}
     image: {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.container.image}}
-    command: [&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;sh&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;-c&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$(ZEPPELIN_HOME)/bin/interpreter.sh -d $(ZEPPELIN_HOME)/interpreter/{{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.group.name}} -r {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.rpc.portRange}} -c {{zeppelin.k8s.server.rpc.service}} -p {{zeppelin.k8s.server.rpc.portRange}} -i {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.group.id}} -l {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.localRepo}} -g {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.setting.name}}&quot;&lt;/span&gt;]
+    command: [&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;sh&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;-c&quot;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;$(ZEPPELIN_HOME)/bin/interpreter.sh -d $(ZEPPELIN_HOME)/interpreter/{{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.group.name}} -r {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.rpc.portRange}} -c {{zeppelin.k8s.server.rpc.service}} -p {{zeppelin.k8s.server.rpc.portRange}} -i {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.group.id}} -l {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.localRepo}}/{{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.setting.name}} -g {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.setting.name}}&quot;&lt;/span&gt;]
     lifecycle:
       preStop:
         exec:
@@ -83,11 +83,16 @@ spec:
     volumeMounts:
     - name: spark
       mountPath: /opt/spark/conf
+    - name: zeppelin-local-repo
+      mountPath: {{zeppelin.k8s.interpreter.localRepo}}
   volumes:
   - name: spark
     configMap:
       defaultMode: 420
       name: spark
+  - name: zeppelin-local-repo
+    persistentVolumeClaim:
+      claimName: zeppelin-local-repo
   {% endif %}
 ---
 kind: Service
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think your proposed solution for the sync process is very good. We should prefer the sync solution.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17322687" author="reamer" created="Fri, 16 Apr 2021 07:33:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Closed with &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4072&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/4072&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                    </comments>
